EXT. BROKEN-DOWN SCHOOL BUS - ROADSIDE - DUSK

Steam hisses from the hood. Six teenagers sit on the shoulder in a ragged line.

FIONN (17, drum sticks in his back pocket) kicks gravel. WANJIRU (17, braids, ukulele case) stares at the road. DEXTER (17, letterman jacket) scrolls his phone. MARGUERITE (16, sketchbook) draws without looking up.  Last, ISOLDE (16, borrowed varsity hoodie) sits apart, arms around her knees.

FIONN
Anyone get a signal?

DEXTER
No.

WANJIRU
^No.

They glance at each other. Neither smiles. Marguerite's pencil stops.

FIONN
We could walk.

MARGUERITE
We could stay.

Nobody says what they mean. Isolde turns her face away.

Headlights swing across the gravel. A battered pickup brakes. The door opens. MR. DELACROIX-HUANG (50s, their old music teacher, thermos in hand) climbs out and surveys the bus.

MR. DELACROIX-HUANG
Anyone hurt?

Silence. Fionn stands. Wanjiru stands. One by one, the others rise. Isolde stays seated until Marguerite offers her a hand without looking at her. She takes it.
